// Command & Conquer: Generals Zero Hour -- Persian (Farsi) game text
//
// Plain UTF-8. One entry is a label line, a quoted string, and END.
// Lines starting with // are comments. Escapes: \n \t \" \\
//
// Translated from the English original (EnglishZH.big, generals.csf) into Persian, with
// colloquial speech where a character or a joke needs it (the American boss speaks
// colloquial Tehrani, Dr. Thrax bought his degree in front of the university). The GLA stays
// "GLA". Uses ZWNJ (U+200C) inside words as Persian spelling requires; the engine shapes and
// lays text out right to left (render2dsentence.cpp) and drops ZWNJ after shaping. Hotkeys
// follow "نام (&K)". Multiplayer map names stay in English. Checked with
// scripts/language/translate_kit.py. See languages/README.md before editing.

GX:LanguageName
"فارسی"
END

